    "about": {
      "type": "detail-folds",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "paper",
        "anchor_id": "what-it-is",
        "eyebrow": "What it is",
        "heading": "What it is",
        "head_note": "<p>A crew-height waterproof sock built in three layers: a knitted lining against your skin, a Porelle® waterproof layer in the middle, and a tough knit on the outside. One height, one build, four colours, four sizes. The same sock whether you bought it for a hill, a commute, a shift or for wudu.</p>",
        "shots_aspect": "1 / 1",
        "cta_label": "Buy a pair",
        "cta_url": "#buy",
        "cta_note": "Back to the top of the page — size, colour and quantity are all there."
      },
      "blocks": {
        "d1": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image_fallback": "diagram-anatomy.jpg",
            "image_alt": "Anatomy diagram of a HydroSox sock labelling the ribbed cuff, breathable mesh panel, seamless toe, heel-fit shaping and non-slip sole.",
            "caption": "Anatomy — cuff, mesh panel, seamless toe, heel-fit"
          }
        },
        "d2": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image_fallback": "diagram-layers.jpg",
            "image_alt": "Cutaway diagram of the three-layer fabric: the Porelle® waterproof barrier, the moisture-management layer, and the breathable inner face.",
            "caption": "The three layers, in section"
          }
        },
        "f1": {
          "type": "fold",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Three-layer construction",
            "note": "The mechanism behind the waterproof claim, layer by layer."
          }
        },
        "w1": {
          "type": "row",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Inner layer",
            "body": "<p>A soft knitted lining that moves sweat off the foot and stops the membrane sitting against the skin.</p>"
          }
        },
        "w2": {
          "type": "row",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Porelle® membrane",
            "body": "<p>A licensed third-party waterproof-breathable membrane — not a name we invented. Water cannot get in; vapour from the foot can get out.</p>"
          }
        },
        "w3": {
          "type": "row",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Outer layer",
            "body": "<p>The knitted face that takes the abrasion inside a boot or shoe, and holds the sock's shape when it is not being worn.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f2": {
          "type": "fold",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What it will not do",
            "note": "The limits are real and physical. No competitor in the mapped set states theirs."
          }
        },
        "w4": {
          "type": "row",
          "settings": {
            "title": "They are not a boot replacement.",
            "body": "<p>One component of a system. If your footwear is wrong for the ground, this will not fix it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "w5": {
          "type": "row",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Water over the cuff gets in.",
            "body": "<p>A sock is open at the top. Go deeper than the cuff and you are wet, and no waterproof sock behaves otherwise.</p>"
          }
        },
        "w6": {
          "type": "row",
          "settings": {
            "title": "They are not indestructible.",
            "body": "<p>A membrane is a membrane. Abrasion, toenails and the wrong wash cycle will eventually end one.</p>"
          }
        },
        "w7": {
          "type": "row",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Breathable does not mean dry inside.",
            "body": "<p>Work hard enough and you will sweat faster than any membrane can move vapour. Breathability slows that. It does not repeal it.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
