            "title": "Washing them won’t ruin them. Heat will.",
            "body": "<p>Cool wash, no fabric softener, no bleach, air dry. A waterproof layer fails from heat, softener and rubbing long before it fails from age.</p>",
            "link_label": "How to wash them",
            "link_url": "/pages/care-and-washing"
          }
        },
        "ab2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Fourteen days, no reason needed.",
            "body": "<p>Unworn and in the original packaging. Your statutory rights are the floor here, not the ceiling — the returns page sets out both.</p>",
            "link_label": "The returns policy",
            "link_url": "/pages/returns-and-refunds"
          }
        },
        "ab3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A fault isn’t the same as wear.",
            "body": "<p>A seam letting water through in the first few weeks is a fault. Thinning at the heel after months is wear. The returns page draws that line honestly.</p>",
            "link_label": "The returns page",
            "link_url": "/pages/returns-and-refunds"
          }
        }
